# Line endings for the block-format data files (Game/Serialize.h).
#
# The game WRITES these with CRLF (serialize::kEol) and reads either, so without
# a rule here their endings would depend on whoever cloned the repo and how
# their core.autocrlf happened to be set. `eol=crlf` pins the working copy to
# what the writer emits, so an editor save is never a whole-file diff.
#
# This clone has core.autocrlf=false, which is why the drift was invisible: the
# catalogs sat at 19 LF files and one CRLF for as long as they had, and only a
# rewrite of one of them would have shown it.
*.cat text eol=crlf
project.ini text eol=crlf
